Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: rtkit: wait 10 s for the boot handshake

On J714s/T6050 with all 15 cores online, nvme-apple logged
"ANS did not boot" / "Reset failure status: -62" about 1.07 s after
RTKit init, leaving the root disk missing. A manual rebind failed the
same way. ANS firmware sometimes needs ~3 s to answer. Workaround from
rolotrealanis98/m5pro-linux patch 0016; applies to every RTKit coprocessor.

---
diff --git i/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit.c w/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit.c
index a863ae166..7459d9c70 100644
--- i/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit.c
+++ w/drivers/soc/apple/rtkit.c
@@ -720,12 +720,20 @@ struct apple_rtkit *apple_rtkit_init(struct device *dev, void *cookie,
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(apple_rtkit_init);
 
+/*
+ * omarchy-m5: T6050's ANS firmware sometimes needs ~3 s to answer the RTKit
+ * handshake on an all-core boot, so 1 s leaves the root disk missing.
+ * Workaround from rolotrealanis98/m5pro-linux; it applies to every RTKit
+ * coprocessor, not just ANS.
+ */
+#define APPLE_RTKIT_HANDSHAKE_TIMEOUT_MS 10000
+
 static int apple_rtkit_wait_for_completion(struct completion *c)
 {
 	long t;
 
 	t = wait_for_completion_interruptible_timeout(c,
-						      msecs_to_jiffies(1000));
+			msecs_to_jiffies(APPLE_RTKIT_HANDSHAKE_TIMEOUT_MS));
 	if (t < 0)
 		return t;
 	else if (t == 0)
